# api-survey-apps — global

## Stack & layout

Turborepo + pnpm workspaces (`apps/*`, `packages/*`). Node `>=24`, `pnpm@11`, all apps/packages use `"type": "module"`.

| App                      | Role                                            | Port |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- | ---- |
| `apps/web` (`web`)       | Next.js 16 admin UI + Clerk                     | 3000 |
| `apps/api` (`api`)       | NestJS HTTP API, BullMQ producers               | 4000 |
| `apps/worker` (`worker`) | NestJS BullMQ consumers (ETL, imports, exports) | 4001 |

| Package                        | Use for                                              |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `@workspace/database`          | Prisma client, enums, RBAC/seed helpers              |
| `@workspace/validation`        | Shared Zod / domain validators                       |
| `@workspace/ui`                | shadcn/Radix components + `globals.css`              |
| `@workspace/jobs`              | BullMQ queue/job name constants + payload types      |
| `@workspace/etl-core`          | Convex→Nest survey ETL (pure transform logic)        |
| `@workspace/excel-reports`     | ExcelJS workbook builders/parsers                    |
| `@workspace/typescript-config` | Shared TSConfigs (`base`, `nextjs`, `react-library`) |
| `@workspace/eslint-config`     | Shared ESLint (`base`, `next-js`, `react-internal`)  |

Root scripts orchestrate via Turbo (`pnpm dev` = api+web+worker). Env lives at **repo root** (`.env.local` → `.env.{NODE_ENV}` → `.env`), not per-app.

## Workspace boundaries

- Prefer `@workspace/*` over duplicating Zod schemas, queue names, Prisma types, or UI primitives inside apps.
- Domain HTTP lives in `apps/api`; background work in `apps/worker`; UI in `apps/web`.
- Schema/migrations only in `packages/database/prisma/`. Import via `@workspace/database` — never reach into `src/generated` from apps.
- Queue contracts only in `@workspace/jobs` — never invent string queue/job names in api/worker.
- Do not put Nest controllers in worker or Prisma repositories in web.

## TypeScript (universal)

- `strict: true` and `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true` (from `@workspace/typescript-config/base.json`).
- Packages/base: `module`/`moduleResolution` = `NodeNext`. Web extends `nextjs.json` (`Bundler`). Nest apps use **local** tsconfigs with decorators (there is no `nestjs.json`).
- No `any`. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing. Exhaustive `switch` with `never` default for unions/enums.
- Nest/api/worker relative imports use **`.js` extensions** (ESM). Web uses `@/` path alias.
- Colocate unit tests as `*.spec.ts` next to source.

## Commands

```bash
pnpm dev                 # api + web + worker
pnpm build && pnpm test && pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint
pnpm db:generate         # Prisma client
pnpm db:migrate          # migrate via @workspace/database
```

## Agent notes

- Next.js 16 differs from older docs — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and root `AGENTS.md` before changing web.
- Product RBAC is Nest permissions (`survey:view`, etc.), not Clerk roles. Clerk only authenticates.
